    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0204" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg882"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Pike.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 5, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Tour despatch of December 17 (No. 68) has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>Your suggestions in regard to the financial measures of the government will
                    receive due consideration.</p>
                <p>You will accept my thanks for the information you have obtained and given to me
                    concerning the case of the rescue of a Dutch vessel, during the Crimean war,
                    when proceeding to port for adjudication, under convoy as a prize, and the
                    demand for her restitution, which was thereupon made by the British
                    government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Pike</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
